# ==========================================================================
# .dockerignore - production build context for the Admin Panel WebApi image
# Keep this file in the solution root (next to Dockerfile and DotNet.sln),
# named exactly ".dockerignore" (no .txt extension).
# Anything listed here is never sent to Docker, never ends up in the image,
# and never invalidates the build cache.
# ==========================================================================

# --- Build output (Visual Studio / dotnet). These contain Windows paths and break Linux builds ---
**/bin
**/obj
**/TestResults
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts

# --- IDE and editor files ---
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.userosscache
**/*.sln.docstates
**/*.DotSettings.user
**/launchSettings.json

# --- Source control and CI (not needed to build the image) ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.azure-pipelines
.editorconfig

# --- Secrets and environment-specific config: NEVER ship these in an image ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/appsettings.Staging.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.snk
**/*.publishsettings
**/*.pubxml
**/*.pubxml.user
**/PublishProfiles
**/dataprotection-keys

# --- Logs, dumps and local data ---
**/logs
**/Logs
**/*.log
**/*.dmp
**/*.mdmp
**/*.bak
**/*.mdf
**/*.ldf
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db

# --- Dependencies installed on the developer machine (restored fresh in the image) ---
**/node_modules
**/.nuget

# --- Docker / deployment files (the Dockerfile is still used by the builder) ---
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml
.dockerignore
deploy.sh
nginx

# --- Docs and notes ---
*.md
*.txt
**/README*
**/CURRENT-JOURNAL.txt

# --- Projects not needed for the WebApi image (it only references Bll, Dll, Utility) ---
HangFireApi
Logging

# --- OS junk ---
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
